# [IMPL-DUPCOMPARE] [ARCH-DUPCOMPARE] [REQ-DUPCOMPARE] Content-duplicate CLI

## RUN_CLI

INPUT: args []string, stdout io.Writer, stderr io.Writer
PRE: args provided by OS
POST: exit code 0, 1, or 2; stdout contains duplicate groups only on success
EFFECTS: reads top-level regular files from two directories; writes formatted text to stdout
FAILURE_MODES: usage_error (exit 1); io_error (exit 2)

1. CALL PARSE_AND_VALIDATE_ARGS
2. files := CALL LIST_TOP_LEVEL_FILES(dir1, dir2)
3. digestMap := empty map[string][]string
4. FOR EACH file IN files:
     digest := CALL HASH_FILE_CONTENTS(file.Path)
     append file.Path to digestMap[digest]
5. groups := CALL GROUP_BY_CONTENT_HASH(digestMap)
6. output := CALL REPORT_DUPLICATE_GROUPS(groups)
7. write output to stdout

## PARSE_AND_VALIDATE_ARGS

INPUT: args excluding program name
PRE: len(args) == 2
POST: dir1 and dir2 are existing directories OR error with exit 1
FAILURE_MODES: wrong_count; not_found; not_directory

1. IF len(args) != 2 THEN write usage to stderr; exit 1
2. FOR EACH path IN args:
     IF path missing THEN error exit 1
     IF path not directory THEN error exit 1

## LIST_TOP_LEVEL_FILES

INPUT: dir1 string, dir2 string
PRE: both directories exist and are readable
POST: []FileRecord with absolute paths for top-level regular files only; dotfiles included
EFFECTS: reads directory entries only
FAILURE_MODES: dir_read_error (exit 2)

1. FOR EACH dir IN [dir1, dir2]:
     FOR EACH entry IN ReadDir(dir):
       IF entry is subdirectory THEN skip
       IF entry is symlink THEN skip
       IF entry is not regular file THEN skip
       append FileRecord{AbsPath} to result
2. RETURN result

## HASH_FILE_CONTENTS

INPUT: path string
PRE: path is readable regular file
POST: lowercase hex SHA-256 digest of full file content
FAILURE_MODES: read_error (exit 2)

1. Open path for reading
2. Stream bytes through sha256 hasher
3. RETURN hex digest

## GROUP_BY_CONTENT_HASH

INPUT: map digest string to []path string
PRE: paths are absolute strings
POST: []DuplicateGroup where len(Paths) >= 2; paths sorted lexicographically within group; groups sorted by first path
DATA_TRANSITION: filter singleton digests

1. FOR EACH digest, paths IN map:
     IF len(paths) < 2 THEN skip
     sort paths lexicographically
     append DuplicateGroup{Name: paths[0], Paths: paths}
2. sort groups by Name
3. RETURN groups

## REPORT_DUPLICATE_GROUPS

INPUT: []DuplicateGroup sorted by group name
POST: formatted string; first path unindented; siblings indented two spaces; newline between groups
TERMINATION: returns when all groups formatted

1. FOR EACH group IN groups:
     write group.Name line
     FOR EACH path IN group.Paths[1:]:
       write two-space indent + path line
     IF not last group THEN write newline separator
2. RETURN complete string with trailing newline when non-empty
